an in this thing which is  both good and bad for me what I see a  ben affleck and his performance i'm  liking and while i feel that a lot of  the destruction and Man of Steel was  rather unnecessary and rather gratuitous  if you're going to have that level of  destruction it's nice to have it mean  something and obviously it's it's now  panning out  it does mean something it impacts the  world and impacts the story impacts  Batman particularly and I find it  interesting the way that they've gotten  him very personally motivated against  Superman I think that can work that said  I was not loving the fact that we saw  glimpses of Batman's origin and his  parents getting killed for crying out  loud we know this story already don't  even give me flashbacks of it well why  are you eating up screen time on that  seeing glimpses of that just makes me  really worried that what we're actually  gonna get is not a batman superman movie  it's going to be a batman movie with  Superman as the plot driver this is  really first time we've seen more Batman  so maybe just this trailer is highlight  any more but the presence of origin  stuff on Batman even being in the movie  that I don't like that at all we got a  few quick glimpses of Wonder Woman not a  lot to go off there yet the little bits  we get of Lex Luthor I'm up and down on  I think I get where jesse eisenberg's  interpretation is going with the  character I think it could work but that  wig man KITT get rid of that thing I  mean we already know he appears as bald  in the movie where that was released as  a publicity still so why are you  sticking that they don't tell me that's  the one takeaway you're going to take  away from the original Christopher Reeve  Superman movie is to have lex luthor in  a dumb wig that he rips off at the end  of the movie the other thing that makes  me nervous is how many shots we got of  Superman where he looks pissed off and  I'm not gonna say Superman can never get  pissed but I really want 